# recompsx.cfg — launch parameters for the Dreamcast build.
#
# A Dreamcast booted from a disc has no command line, so this file is where the arguments come
# from. The backend looks for it at /pc/recompsx.cfg (the development host, over dcload), then
# /cd/RECOMPSX.CFG, then /cd/recompsx.cfg. Launched over dcload with a real command line, that
# command line wins and this file is not read at all.
#
# One argument per line, in the order the program expects them. Nothing is split on spaces, so a
# path with a space in it needs no quoting. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Copy this to the root of the disc (or next to dc-tool) as recompsx.cfg and edit the paths.

# 1. the PS-EXE the recompiler was built from
/cd/BOOT.EXE

# 2. the disc image — a BIN/CUE or ISO, or a directory of files already extracted from one
/cd/DISC.BIN

# Options may follow, exactly as on a desktop command line. Uncomment to stop at frame 600 and
# print one digest instead of playing, which is how a console is compared against JavaScript.
# --headless-hash
# 600
